      "title": "Full year 2026 earnings released: EPS: ₹34.67 (vs ₹33.70 in FY 2025)",
      "body": "Full year 2026 results: EPS: ₹34.67 (up from ₹33.70 in FY 2025). Revenue: ₹32.1b (down 27% from FY 2025). Net income: ₹13.1b (up 3.0% from FY 2025). Profit margin: 41% (up from 29% in FY 2025). The increase in margin was driven by lower expenses. Revenue is forecast to grow 21% p.a. on average during the next 3 years, compared to a 1.1% growth forecast for the Banks industry in India. Over the last 3 years on average, earnings per share has fallen by 12% per year but the company’s share price has increased by 25% per year, which means it is well ahead of earnings.",
